## 3. Understanding the two shortcuts

The project uses two separate shortcuts.

### Start

The `Start` shortcut is used to create the initial Wallet pass.

Run this first when setting up the project for the first time.

Once the pass has been created, you should not need to create another pass every time your QR code changes.

### Generate PureGym

The `Generate PureGym` shortcut refreshes the QR code on your existing Wallet pass.

It is not intended to create a new pass every time it runs.

The shortcut uses four configuration values:

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Email | Your PureGym login email |
| PIN | Your PureGym login password or PIN |
| WalletWallet Pass Number | Identifies the pass to update |
| WalletWallet API key | Authorises the WalletWallet update request |

Make sure each value is entered in the correct Text action.

### Why the pass number matters

The WalletWallet pass number identifies the pass that should receive the updated QR code.

If the pass number is missing or incorrect, the shortcut may generate a valid PureGym QR code but fail when attempting to update WalletWallet.

The pass number should be copied from the WalletWallet pass URL or the value provided during your initial pass setup.

Do not confuse the pass number with your PureGym membership number.

