## 7. Apple Wallet problems

### The pass will not add to Apple Wallet

If the pass is generated but does not open in Wallet:

- Check that the pass was downloaded correctly.
- Make sure the file is a valid Apple Wallet pass.
- Try opening the pass from Safari or the Files app.
- Check that the pass was generated by the intended shortcut.

A pass file normally uses the `.pkpass` extension.

### The pass appears but has no barcode

Check that the pass contains a barcode and that the barcode value was supplied correctly.

If the pass was created before the QR code was retrieved, run `Generate PureGym` to update it.

### The pass is duplicated

If you accidentally run `Start` multiple times, you may create multiple passes.

Remove the unwanted pass from Apple Wallet and keep the pass whose WalletWallet pass number is configured in your refresh shortcut.

Do not create a new pass every time you want to refresh the QR code.

### The pass displays an old QR code

Run `Generate PureGym` manually.

If the QR code updates successfully, check your automation settings.

If it does not update, check the PureGym authentication and WalletWallet request separately.

